<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 176 0 R
/T (Are guests allowed to bring their own reusable containers \(i.e., Tupperware, coolers, water bottles, etc.\) for vendors to fill with their food and beverage products?)
/E (Are guests allowed to bring their own reusable containers \(i.e., Tupperware, coolers, water bottles, etc.\) for vendors to fill with their food and beverage products?)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
582 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 176 0 R
/T (Yes! Encouraging guests to bring reusable items is one of the most effective ways to reduce waste. While recycling and composting are crucial to a zero waste event, the best way to minimize landfill impact is by preventing waste in the first place. Speak with your vendors beforehand to discuss whether they can accommodate customers bringing their own containers, and consider offering incentives, like small discounts, for guests who bring their own.)
/E (Yes! Encouraging guests to bring reusable items is one of the most effective ways to reduce waste. While recycling and composting are crucial to a zero waste event, the best way to minimize landfill impact is by preventing waste in the first place. Speak with your vendors beforehand to discuss whether they can accommodate customers bringing their own containers, and consider offering incentives, like small discounts, for guests who bring their own.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
583 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 176 0 R
/T (Does the city have ways to accurately determine the amount of waste and recycling that is generated at a zero waste event?)
/E (Does the city have ways to accurately determine the amount of waste and recycling that is generated at a zero waste event?)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
584 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 176 0 R
/T (As this is a new initiative, there are currently limited ways to generate estimates of how much waste has been diverted away from landfills, either through reduction or recycling. Fortunately, there are ways to approximate these values based on the number of guests, the type of event, how many containers are used, and by weight of materials. Using these values as proxies, data can be determined and used to measure the success of a zero waste event. Certain haulers and consulting services can provide these numbers for you.)
/E (As this is a new initiative, there are currently limited ways to generate estimates of how much waste has been diverted away from landfills, either through reduction or recycling. Fortunately, there are ways to approximate these values based on the number of guests, the type of event, how many containers are used, and by weight of materials. Using these values as proxies, data can be determined and used to measure the success of a zero waste event. Certain haulers and consulting services can provide these numbers for you.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [10]
>>
